	"rows": [
		{
			"id": "eAzQKd_YNDPnneGjS",
			"description": "Inferno Boltgun",
			"local_notes": "The warpflame follow-up applies only when the bolt penetrates DR, as for the Godwyn boltgun's explosive follow-up (B414).\n\nLore: The inferno boltgun fires bolts charged with warpflame, and is the usual weapon of the Rubric Marines of the Thousand Sons. The fiction describes bolts that burn with a sorcerous fire as well as exploding (Black Library Thousand Sons fiction; Codex: Thousand Sons). Few outside the Legion have the sorcery to make the ammunition.\n\nDesign: Handling is the Godwyn boltgun's, copied as the task and framework direct: Acc 4, range 200/1000, RoF 3, 24(3) shots, ST 19, Bulk -5, Rcl 3, Guns (Rifle), 38 lb. Damage follows the Chaos anchor in framework.md: 6dx2 pi++ as the boltgun, one divisor step further, (3) against (2), and a 2d burn follow-up in place of 2d cr ex. The follow-up is a second line whose usage contains \"follow-up\" and sits right after the main line, the pattern the simulator links. By exact dice, against an Astartes Mark VII (DR 100, effective DR 33) the main bolt penetrates 85.5% of the time, against the Mark IV (DR 95) 90.4%, against carapace 99%, and against Tartaros Terminator plate (DR 190) 0.5%. The standard boltgun manages 14.5% against Mark VII, so the divisor step makes it a weapon that kills Astartes, which suits a weapon built to kill sealed armour. Cost is $3,000 against the boltgun's $1,200 because the ammunition is sorcerous. LC 0: Imperial law bans it outright.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Chaos",
				"Tzeentch",
				"Thousand Sons"
			],
			"tech_level": "10",
			"legality_class": "0",
			"base_value": "3000",
			"base_weight": "38 lb",
