		{
			"id": "ebhvvW8RBzkgkBwav",
			"description": "Warpflamer",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Tzeentch's sorcerers and the Thousand Sons use flamers that spit warpflame, a fire of changing colours that burns by the will of the warp, not by fuel. The Codex entries for Chaos Space Marines and Thousand Sons give it as a flamer with a deadlier flame.\n\nDesign: The Flamer's profile, copied: 4d burn cone, 5 yards, 4(5) shots, ST 9, Bulk -3, Liquid Projector (Flamethrower), 14 lb. Per the Chaos anchor in framework.md the ablaze follow-up is 2d burn per turn, up from the Flamer's 1d, because warpflame does not burn out. The usage text \"per turn while ablaze\" is the one the simulator reads as ongoing fire. TL 8 matches the Flamer; the cost is $1,500 against $550 for the sorcery involved. LC 0.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Chaos",
				"Tzeentch"
			],
			"tech_level": "8",
			"legality_class": "0",
			"base_value": "1500",
			"base_weight": "14 lb",
			"weapons": [
				{
					"id": "WY_xsIfy_QW7dF_Bm",
					"sv": 1,
					"damage": {
						"type": "burn",
						"base": "4d"
					},
					"range": "5",
					"shots": "4(5)",
					"bulk": "-3",
					"strength": "9†",
					"usage": "Cone attack (5 yards)",
					"usage_notes": "No Acc bonus applies and no aiming roll is needed against a target inside the cone, as for the Flamer and the Basic Set Flamethrower (B281). Treat cover bonuses as halved (round down) against the cone.",
					"defaults": [
						{
