		{
			"id": "efOU7W3jP-ZSUqxQt",
			"description": "Sonic Blaster",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Noise Marines of the Emperor's Children carry sonic blasters, rifle-sized weapons that project a beam of destructive sound which shakes a target's body apart inside its armour (Codex: Chaos Space Marines, Emperor's Children and Noise Marine fiction). Their sound-obsessed users prize the shriek of a fired shot as much as its effect.\n\nDesign: Damage and rate follow the Chaos anchor: 6d(5) cr, RoF 3, range 50/150. The divisor is what lets sound shake a Marine apart inside his armour, as in the fiction; 5d(3) could never get through Mark VII plate. History: 6d(5) with Acc 5 and Rcl 1 won 38 fights in 40 against loyalist Marines under the early AI; 5d(5) with Acc 4 and Rcl 2 then fell to 8 in 60 once the AI stopped wasting turns, because each hit did a third of a bolt's injury (10.6 against 32.6) and almost never a major wound. 6d(5) with Acc 4 and Rcl 2 wins 48 in 60, just under a Legionary with a boltgun (92%): a bolter-class gun, as in the fiction. Handling follows framework.md's Weapon handling stats. Weight 24 lb: an Astartes-scale rifle, lighter than the 38 lb Godwyn boltgun because it carries no heavy bolt and propellant. Minimum ST is the square root of 10 times 24, about 15.5, which rounds to 16, with the † for two-handed use. Acc 4: a rifle value. Rcl 2: it throws no mass, but the sound projector bucks; less than a bolter's 3. Bulk -5, an Astartes-pattern rifle. Shots 30(3) from an energy cell. Skill is Guns (Rifle), as the task requires: sound is not a beam in the framework's Skills table, and the weapon is a shoulder rifle. By exact dice, 6d(5) beats Mark VII plate (effective DR 20) on 55% of hits, its neck seal (DR 12) on 98% and carapace (DR 14) on 94%, and never Terminator plate (DR 40).",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Chaos",
				"Slaanesh",
				"Noise Marine"
			],
			"tech_level": "10",
			"legality_class": "0",
			"base_value": "2500",
			"base_weight": "24 lb",
			"weapons": [
				{
					"id": "WTMvCMuy9TBNnkvXh",
					"sv": 1,
					"damage": {
						"type": "cr",
						"base": "6d",
						"armor_divisor": 5
					},
					"accuracy": "4",
					"range": "50/150",
					"rate_of_fire": "3",
					"shots": "30(3)",
					"bulk": "-5",
					"recoil": "2",
					"strength": "16†",
					"usage": "Standard",
					"usage_notes": "The sound shakes the wearer inside the armour. By default nothing extra applies, but the GM may add the blunt trauma rule (B379) to a hit that fails to penetrate.",
