		{
			"id": "eA4m2L1KU8qemcmKs",
			"description": "Plague Knife",
			"local_notes": "Sized for a gauntleted Astartes hand, like the Astartes combat knife. Knife edge (house rule): reduces the penalty for targeting chinks in armor (p. B400) by 2, as the stiletto does (MA228).\n\nLore: Death Guard Plague Marines carry blades that are crusted with filth and rot, poisoned with the diseases of Nurgle. A scratch from one carries a plague (Codex: Death Guard and Black Library Death Guard fiction).\n\nDesign: The thrust and swing lines are the Astartes combat knife's, copied: thr+1 imp and sw+1 cut, reach C,1, parry 0, ST 11, Shortsword, 4 lb. The follow-up is the Chaos anchor, a 2d tox line whose usage contains \"follow-up\" so the simulator applies it after a penetrating hit. Cost $600 over the combat knife's $200 for the poison. TL 2 as the knife: the blade is ordinary, the corruption is not. Monoedge rule (user direction): as the Astartes combat knife it is built on, armour divisor (3).",
			"tags": [
				"Melee Weapon",
				"Chaos",
				"Nurgle",
				"Death Guard"
			],
